  "result": "Set up and verified. Structure:\n\n- `go.mod` — module `syscli`, requires `golang.org/x/sys v0.48.0`\n- `main.go` — CLI entry point, calls the platform-agnostic `diskFree(path)`\n- `diskfree_unix.go` (`//go:build linux || darwin`) — implements it via `unix.Statfs`\n- `diskfree_windows.go` (`//go:build windows`) — implements it via `windows.GetDiskFreeSpaceEx`\n\nIt builds natively on Linux and cross-compiles clean for `darwin/arm64` and `windows/amd64`, and the Linux binary runs correctly (reports free/total bytes for `.`). This demonstrates the pattern for any low-level syscall not in stdlib: put the shared logic/signature in `main.go`, and split per-OS implementations into build-tagged files backed by `golang.org/x/sys/unix` or `golang.org/x/sys/windows`.",
